# Bonsol Interface Standards

## Context
- Applied when working with Bonsol protocol messages and types
- Focuses on FlatBuffers serialization and version handling
- Ensures consistent handling of protocol messages
- Critical for cross-language compatibility
- Particularly important for RISC0 v1.2.1 integration

## Requirements

### Version Handling
- Use `ProverVersion` enum for version compatibility:
  ```rust
  match version {
      ProverVersion::V1_2_1 { verifier_digest } => {
          // Handle current version
      }
      ProverVersion::V1_0_1 { .. } => {
          // Handle legacy version
      }
      ProverVersion::UnsupportedVersion => {
          // Handle unsupported version
      }
  }
  ```
- Validate version compatibility early:
  - Check prover version before processing requests
  - Use `try_into()` for converting from FlatBuffers version
  - Handle version mismatches with appropriate errors

### FlatBuffers Message Handling
- Use proper unpacking patterns:
  ```rust
  // Reading messages
  let claim = root_as_claim_v1(buffer)?;
  
  // Accessing fields safely
  if let Some(execution_id) = claim.execution_id() {
      // Process execution_id
  }
  
  // Unpacking to owned data when needed
  let claim_t = claim.unpack();
  ```
- Validate required fields:
  - Check for None values in optional fields
  - Handle missing data appropriately
  - Use early returns for validation

### Protocol Messages
- Handle core message types correctly:
  - `ClaimV1`: Execution claims and commitments
  - `DeployV1`: Program deployment data
  - `ExecutionRequestV1`: Execution requests
- Follow field access patterns:
  - Use direct field access for required fields
  - Check optional fields with if let
  - Unpack data only when owned values needed

## Examples

<example>
// Good: Complete message handling with validation
fn process_execution_request(data: &[u8]) -> Result<()> {
    // 1. Parse and validate message
    let request = root_as_execution_request_v1(data)
        .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidData)?;
        
    // 2. Validate version
    let version: ProverVersion = request
        .prover_version()
        .try_into()
        .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidVersion)?;
        
    if version != VERSION_V1_2_1 {
        return Err(Error::VersionMismatch);
    }
    
    // 3. Process required fields
    let execution_id = request
        .execution_id()
        .ok_or(Error::MissingExecutionId)?;
        
    // 4. Handle optional fields safely
    let callback = if let Some(program_id) = request.callback_program_id() {
        Some(ProgramExec {
            program_id: program_id.try_into()?,
            instruction_prefix: request
                .callback_instruction_prefix()
                .map(|v| v.bytes().to_vec())
                .unwrap_or_default(),
        })
    } else {
        None
    };
    
    Ok(())
}
</example>

<example>
// Good: Version handling with metrics
fn validate_prover_version(version: ProverVersion) -> Result<()> {
    match version {
        ProverVersion::V1_2_1 { verifier_digest } 
            if verifier_digest == DIGEST_V1_2_1_BYTES => {
            emit_event!(MetricEvents::VersionValidation,
                version => "1.2.1",
                status => "success"
            );
            Ok(())
        }
        other => {
            emit_event!(MetricEvents::VersionValidation,
                version => format!("{:?}", other),
                status => "failed"
            );
            Err(Error::InvalidVersion)
        }
    }
}
</example>

<example type="invalid">
// Bad: Unsafe field access
fn process_claim_unsafe(data: &[u8]) -> Result<String> {
    let claim = root_as_claim_v1(data)?;
    Ok(claim.execution_id().to_string()) // Missing None check
}
</example>

<example type="invalid">
// Bad: Missing version validation
fn handle_request(request: ExecutionRequestV1) {
    // Directly processing without version check
    process_execution(request);
}
</example>

## Critical Notes
<critical>
- ALWAYS validate prover version before processing
- NEVER assume optional fields are present
- Handle FlatBuffers errors appropriately
- Unpack only when owned data needed
- Use proper error types for protocol errors
- Include version checks in metrics
</critical> 